learnings:
  - 'The whole v7 validated its own thesis in microcosm: the adversarial-review step caught that the keystone''s learning-wiring claims were false against the code (fabricated confidence_before, CLI orchestrator doesn''t share completeTask, circular JPS) BEFORE any code shipped. Cross-check before commit is the practice v7 institutionalizes, and it paid off on v7 itself.'
  - 'Per-round rigor held across 7 rounds: every round built + full-suite-green + lore + changelog + commit + push. paradigm-mcp grew 313→373 tests, all green; CLI 387. Discipline over a marathon beats a heroic untested dump.'
  - 'Builders repeatedly cut off mid-report on large orchestration.ts edits (~90k tokens) — the work landed but the final summary truncated. Mitigation: verify state directly (git diff + build + test) rather than trusting the agent''s report; prefer new-file-heavy scoping over giant single-file edits to dodge the limit.'
